-- title:
--   Rigidity of homomorphisms of formal groups modulo a nilpotent ideal
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring and $k$ a field in the same universe, and let $\pi \colon R \to k$ be a surjective ring homomorphism such that $(\ker \pi)^{\mu+1} = 0$ for some natural number $\mu$. Let $p$ be a prime and suppose $k$ has characteristic $p$. Let $F$ be an $m$-dimensional formal group law over $R$, that is, an $m$-tuple of power series in the variables indexed by $\mathrm{Fin}\,m \oplus \mathrm{Fin}\,m$ with vanishing constant terms, with the $i$-th series having linear coefficients $\delta_{ij}$ in each of the two groups of variables, and satisfying the associativity identity, and assume $F$ is commutative, i.e. invariant under swapping the two groups of variables; let $G$ be such a formal group law of dimension $n$, likewise commutative. Let $h$ be a natural number and assume that the quotient of $k[[X_1,\dots,X_m]]$ by the ideal generated by the components of the $p$-th iterate series $(\bar F)^{[p]}$ of the reduction $\bar F =$ `F.map π` (defined by iterating $a \mapsto \bar F(a, X)$ from $0$, i.e. multiplication by $p$) has $k$-dimension $p^h$. Then any two homomorphisms $\theta_1, \theta_2 \colon F \to G$ — each an $n$-tuple of power series in $m$ variables with zero constant term satisfying $\theta(F(X,Y)) = G(\theta(X), \theta(Y))$ — whose components have equal images under $\pi$ coefficientwise are equal.
--
--   This is the rigidity statement of Katz's Serre–Tate local moduli (Lemma 1.1.3(1)) in the several-variable setting: homomorphisms between formal group laws over a ring with nilpotent kernel are determined by their reductions, once the source has finite height after reduction. It is used in the study of deformations of special formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-modules in the Čerednik–Drinfel'd part of the development, for instance to show that deformations over the dual numbers admit no non-trivial automorphisms reducing to the identity.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_MvFormalGroup_Hom_eq_of_map_eq_of_ker_pow_eq_bot_of_finrank_eq_pow.lean

